00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:05.510 align:start position:0%
the aftermath of a shooting attack in  central tel aviv  a gunman arrived at this bar spraying  bullets more than a dozen people were  rushed to hospital  i was heading north and as we were  passing by a bar shot started outside i  saw the window shattering suddenly  people started running and i felt back  pain i did not know there was an injury  i was just walking and then i felt a lot  of blood i saw blood  diesengoff street is usually busy with  people visiting its bars and cafes  by the end of first evening it was full  of security forces you can see right  behind us a restaurant families and  friends were sitting having a supper and  drinks and all of a sudden the  terrorists came over and shot them shot  10 innocent  people  and  injured them unfortunately two of them  were  murdered  israel was already on its highest alert  this was the fourth attack within the  country in recent weeks all of them  appeared to have been carried out by  individuals no palestinian group claimed  a responsibility for any of them  it's understood that neither the  palestinian leadership nor israel wanted  escalation right now in the  long-standing conflict here  but as in the past even when no one's  interested in escalation things can  suddenly spiral out of control perhaps  sooner rather than later for israeli  prime minister naftali bennett who said  he won't engage in peace talks with the  palestinians he's trying to hold  together a fragile coalition which has  just lost its parliamentary majority the  pressure that's sure to fall on him to  adopt tougher measures towards  palestinians could now weaken and divide  his government further  john holman al jazeera west jerusalem
 

